<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - TOYOTA H1 SHR RISES, DIV FLAT.</title>
<headline>TABLE - TOYOTA H1 SHR RISES, DIV FLAT.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		  167.0	  vs	144.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    24.0	  vs	24.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	     67.91	  vs	58.64</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    102.81	  vs	93.52</p>
<p>    Tax			   37.48	  vs	37.23</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     17.62	  vs	45.03</p>
<p>    Turnover		 3,099.67	  vs	2,807.19</p>
<p>    Share of associates'     2.59	  vs	2.35</p>
<p>Div payable September 12</p>
<p>on register August 29</p>
<p>Full name: Toyota South Africa Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Toyota said NAAMSA forecasts of car sales for the whole of 1997 was 373,300 units which was 5.0 percent less than in 1996. Toyota said it aimed to achieve a local market share of about 25.9 percent for the full year.</p>
<p>It said it expected profitability for the year to be below that of 1996 due mainly to the reduction in total market, severe competition, cost pressures and the continuing buying down tendency in the market.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
